<title>GERMANY: Huettenwerke Kayser cuts copper premiums for 1997.</title>
<headline>Huettenwerke Kayser cuts copper premiums for 1997.</headline>
<dateline>LUENEN, Germany 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Huettenwerke Kayser AG said on Wednesday it would cut its copper premiums for 1997 to $27 a tonne over the average of London Metal Exchange settlement prices, from $30 a tonne this year.</p>
<p>The premium for unknown pricing of dg-Rhein-Rod will be $40 a tonne.</p>
<p>Huettenwerke Kayser said that after an intensive investment programme it now had a production capacity of 170,000 tonnes of grade-A electrolytic copper cathodes.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
